    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite is just the one `AcceptanceTest`, and it passes with **BUILD SUCCESS**. Compilation of the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` and the MapStruct mapper (which now maps `customerCode` automatically via the new getter) all succeeded.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, keeping structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods:\n\n1. **New `OwnerCustomerCodePolicy`** (`service/`) \u2014 a self-contained static helper mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephonePolicy` pattern. `LAST3` = upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`; `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits via `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`. Its only surrounding context is its own tiny class, so its WMC_other is near zero.\n\n2. **`Owner`** \u2014 added a `customerCode` field with a plain getter/setter (JPA `@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`). The getter lets MapStruct populate the DTO automatically; the setter is used by the policy.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one added line calling the policy (right beside the existing telephone-policy call) plus one import. The existing method's cyclomatic complexity is unchanged.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema so it's serialized in `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n5. **hsqldb `schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column and a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional seed inserts (the test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`). This follows the same precedent as the earlier `registration_date` change, which was likewise only applied to the hsqldb schema.\n\nThe sequence is global and monotonic, so consecutive creates (`SMI-000X`, `JON-000X+1`) satisfy the test's ordering assertion.",
